BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:165540@iso-ne.com
DTSTAMP:20261005T135909Z
DTSTART:20261001T153200Z
SUMMARY:The Q3 2026 Critical Path Schedule (CPS) update for non-commercial resources is now due
DESCRIPTION:Pursuant to the ISO New England Inc. Transmission\, Markets\, and Services Tariff Section III.13.3\, the Q3 2026 CPS update is now due for those non-commercial resources that either cleared in a Forward Capacity Auction or requested monitoring of their CPS. Please submit the update under the Monitored CPS tab in the Forward Capacity Tracking System (FCTS) for all applicable Capacity Commitment Periods as appropriate. The update should be submitted by the end of Wednesday October 7\, 2026 (by 23:59).\n\n\n\nPursuant to Section III.13.3.2.2 of the ISO New England Inc. Transmission\, Markets\, and Services Tariff\, "for each critical path schedule milestone achieved since the submission of the previous critical path schedule report\, the Project Sponsor must include in the critical path schedule report documentation demonstrating that the milestone has been achieved by the date indicated". This section of the ISO New England Inc. Transmission\, Markets\, and Services Tariff also provides detailed examples of the type of documentation that can be included to demonstrate completion of each milestone.\n\n\n\nReview the Critical Path Schedule Report Training presentation here: https://www.iso-ne.com/static-assets/documents/2019/04/cps_monitoring.htm for guidance on submitting the CPS report in FCTS. If you experience any technical issues while submitting the report or if you have any questions regarding this message\, please contact the Participant Support and Solutions Team by submitting a case via Ask ISO<https://askiso.iso-ne.com/s/contactsupport>\, emailing AskISO@iso-ne.com<mailto:AskISO@iso-ne.com> or by phone at (413) 540-4220.\nhttps://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165540
URL:https://www.iso-ne.com/event-details?eventId=165540
END:VEVENT
